docs/design-notes.md:3378:     it is neither re-enqueued nor marked processed. Since rescan_pcaps() only runs at startup and on IN_Q_OVERFLOW, a transient tshark failure can silently lose that capture forever.
docs/design-notes.md:3379:  2. rescan_pcaps() always discards the newest candidate file, which can permanently skip data. In be/src/pcap_watch.h:212, filenames.pop_back() unconditionally drops the lexicographically last file. That is a
docs/design-notes.md:3380:     reasonable safety heuristic while dumpcap is live, but if stm starts after capture stopped, or if an overflow happens during a quiet period, that last fully-closed file is never processed because no later
